Consider:
```java
public class Test {
    private int val;
    public Test(int val) { this.val = val; }
    public boolean equals(Object other) {
        if (other instanceof Test) {
            return this.val == ((Test) other).val;
        }
        return false;
    }
}
```
What will `new Test(5).equals(new Test(5))` return?

Consider:
```java
class Alpha { public void show() { System.out.print("A"); } }
class Beta extends Alpha { public void show() { super.show(); System.out.print("B"); } }
class Gamma extends Beta { public void show() { super.show(); System.out.print("G"); } }
```
What is printed by: `Alpha obj = new Gamma(); obj.show();`?
